          "sourceRoman": "beḷigge nimma nitya karmānuṣṭhānagaḷaēnide ellavannu mugisi dēvara pūjeyannu pūrṇavāgi mugisi halige athavā maṁṭapadra maṁṭapadalli raṁgōle kemmaṇṇu māḍi pustakagaḷu śāstra pustakagaḷu ēnide nimma hattirali ā pustakagaḷannella ā haligeyalli alaṁkāravanna māḍi adakke gajavastradi ḷa vastragaḷu hūveyiṁda alaṁkāravanna māḍi sarasvatiya pratime athavā sarasvatiya paṭa iddarū sari vēdavyāsa dēvara paṭa adanna muṁbhāgadalli iṭṭu pūjegaḷanna māḍi muṁbhāgadalli iṭṭu pūjegaḷanna māḍabēku pūjege ariśina kuṁkuma gaṁdha maṁtrākṣate ",
          "english": "In the morning, finish all your daily obligatory practices and complete the worship of the deity. On a plank or in a pavilion, prepare the setting with rangoli and red earth [rangoḷe/kemmaṇṇu, recovered by both acoustic passes]. Arrange and decorate the books—the scriptural books that you have—on that plank. Decorate with the stated cloth, flowers and adornment [gajavastrādi, the recorded cloth-adornment name retained]. A Saraswati image or a Saraswati picture is suitable. Place a picture of Vedavyasa in front and perform the worship. Place it in front and perform the worship. For the worship, prepare turmeric, kumkuma, gandha and mantrakshata.",
          "notes": "At116.079s the native word is ariśina (turmeric); fine window3 instead recognizes aṣṭagandha, and the coarse pass has a noisy aṣṭanā join. Turmeric is retained from the explicit native marker; the divergent acoustic recognition is preserved in the clause audit.",
